        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Anarchism</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1840 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Thinkers</span><span class="info-stat-val">William Godwin, of philosophical anarchism; Max Stirner, of individualism; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-joseph-proudhon">Pierre-Joseph Proudhon</a>, first to call himself an anarchist and theorist of mutualism; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-bakunin">Mikhail Bakunin</a>, founder of collectivist anarchism; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-kropotkin">Peter Kropotkin</a>, Russian philosopher and scientist and theorist of anarcho-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communism">communism</a>; Errico Malatesta and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emma-goldman">Emma Goldman</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-tolstoy">Leo Tolstoy</a>, Christian anarchist</span></div>
